@startuml
title YPS TopUp - Swimlane with Cache TTL Strategy (Improved)

|YPS External|
start
:Send YPS Bill Data;

|YPS Entry Service|
:Receive Request;
:Validate Signature & Required Fields;

if (Invalid?) then (Yes)
    :Return FAIL Response;
    stop
endif

:Load from Redis Cache;

note right
Cache TTL Strategy:
- Product → 24h
- Bill → 6h
- Store → 1h
- WorkShift → No cache / 5min
end note

if (Cache Miss?) then (Yes)
    :Load from Database;

    :Update Redis Cache;

    note right
    Cache-Aside Pattern:
    1. Read → Redis
    2. Miss → DB
    3. Save → Redis (with TTL)
    end note
endif

:Build SaleEvent;

:Save Event to Outbox Table;

note right
Outbox Pattern:
- DB + Outbox in same transaction
- Ensure no data loss
end note

:Return SUCCESS Response (Async);

|Outbox Publisher|
:Poll Outbox Table;
:Publish Event to MQ;

:Mark as Published;

|Message Queue (RabbitMQ/Kafka)|
:Queue / Topic;

|Sale Service (Consumer)|
:Consume SaleEvent;

:Check Idempotency;

note right
Idempotency:
- Use transactionSerialNumber
- Prevent duplicate transaction
end note

if (Duplicate?) then (Yes)
    :Ignore Message;
    stop
endif

:Process Sale Transaction;

:Save to Database;

if (Fail?) then (Yes)
    :Retry Message;

    if (Max Retry Exceeded?) then (Yes)
        :Move to DLQ;
    endif

    stop
endif

:Publish Print Event;

|Print Service|
:Consume Print Event;
:Generate Print Data;
:Store Print Info;

stop
@enduml
